== Red Fire Place ==
{{infobox entity
 | name    = Red Fire Place
 | variant = 1
}}

* Can shoot red projectiles at medium speed at Isaac.
** {{dlc|nr}} They do not telegraph before firing projectiles.
** {{Dlc|r}} Red Fire Places have a bounce animation before firing.
** {{dlc|r}} They fire a projectile only once until Isaac re-enters the room.
* Shots fired from a Red Fire Place will not spawn directly on the Red Fire Place, but rather near the fire.
** If Isaac stands too close when a Red Fire Place shoots, the projectile will spawn on Isaac.
** {{Dlc|nr}} {{i|Pyromaniac}} makes Isaac immune to these projectiles.
* Can be extinguished like normal Fire Places.
* 25% chance to drop [[coin]]s (75% chance) or [[heart]]s (25% chance) when extinguished.
** {{dlc|r}} The chance to drop a reward is reduced to 10% while playing on Hard Mode.
* Can rarely replace normal Fire Places.
* {{dlc|a}} Rarely, they'll appear in a room that needs to be cleared by pressing {{E|Pressure Plate}}s. When all are pressed, the Red Fire Places will turn into normal Fire Places.
{{clear}}

== Blue Fire Place ==
{{infobox entity
 | name    = Blue Fire Place
 | variant = 2
}}

* 25% chance to drop a {{E|Soul Heart}} when extinguished.
** {{dlc|r}} The chance to drop a Soul Heart is reduced to 10% while playing on Hard Mode.
* Can only be put out by the following:
** Bombs/explosions and rock blasts (such as from {{i|Wait What?}}).
** {{i|Little Horn|a+nr}} tears.
** {{dlc|r}} Teleporting on top of it with {{i|Stitches|n}}.
** {{dlc+|r}} Using {{i|Suplex!}} on it, then leaving and re-entering the room (likely a bug).
** {{dlc|r+}} Making contact with an explosive locust made from {{i|Abyss}}.
{{dlc-}}
{{clear}}

== Purple Fire Place ==
{{infobox entity
 | name    = Purple Fire Place
 | variant = 3
}}

* Fires purple homing projectiles at Isaac.
** {{dlc|nr}} The homing projectiles deal a full heart of damage.
** {{dlc|r}} They fire a projectile only once until Isaac re-enters the room.
* 25% chance to drop a {{E|Soul Heart}} when extinguished.
** {{dlc|r}} The chance to drop a Soul Heart is reduced to 10% while playing on Hard Mode.
* Can only be put out the same way as Blue Fire Places.
* Can rarely replace Blue Fire Places.
* {{dlc|a}} Rarely, they'll appear in a room that needs to be cleared by pressing {{E|Pressure Plate}}s. When all are pressed, the Purple Fire Places will turn blue.
{{clear}}

== White Fire Place ==
{{infobox entity
 | dlc     = r
 | name    = White Fire Place
 | variant = 4
}}

* Only spawns in specific rooms on {{s|Downpour}} II or {{s|Dross}} II, and there will only be one of these rooms on the floor. The room may contain multiple white fire places depending on the layout.
** {{r|Red Room}}s in {{s|Downpour}} I/II or {{s|Dross}} I/II also have a chance to contain white fire places.
* When Isaac touches the flame, he "dies" and becomes a ghost, which has the properties of {{C|The Lost}} (flight, spectral tears, no health, and the {{I|Holy Mantle}}).
** The ghost will not have Holy Mantle if it is not yet [[Greed Donation Machine#Greed Donation Machine Rewards|unlocked]] for The Lost.
** The ghost will not have Holy Mantle if the room has not been cleared.
** The ghost can take a devil deal for free like The Lost can.
** The ghost can collect health pickups, but these are applied to the main character once Isaac reverts to normal form.
* While a ghost, Isaac can enter the [[mirrored world]] by walking into the mirror found on Downpour/Dross II.
* Completing and exiting a hostile room outside of the mirror world will change Isaac back to normal.
** However, traveling to the next floor as the ghost will not change Isaac back until a room is cleared on that floor.
* As a ghost, the fire can be flown through as if it were an empty tile, with no other effects.
* Can be extinguished by using {{p|Chaos Card}} or by an explosion under the effect of {{i|Astral Projection}} (bug) or {{i|Suplex!}} (bug).
{{clear}}{{dlc clear}}
* Can also be extinguished by using {{p|Soul of Judas}}; quickly running to hover over the White Fire Place then shooting on the white fire place. Upon leaving and re-entering the room, the White Fire Place will be extinguished.

== Notes ==
* All types of fire places deal 16 damage to enemies that come in contact with them.
* {{dlc+|r}} Normal and Red Fire Places are automatically extinguished in flooded rooms (including most rooms in {{s|Flooded Caves}}). Using {{I|Flush!}} will immediately put out all Normal and Red Fire Places in the room.{{dlc-}}
* Unlike similar room obstacles, bombing a fire place will not create a walkable area over a pit.
* {{i|Hot Bombs}} makes Isaac immune to contact damage with fire places. Fire place projectiles will still deal damage.

